      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I've been testing to get the Phys Bones working with the rotation constraint, successfully in scenario 2. ⬅️\n\n⚙️❌ Options I've tried unsuccessfully:\n\n· It doesn't matter if you use Unity's \"Rotation Constraint\" component or VRC Rotation Constraint.\n\n· Changing the Phys Bones version from 1.1 to 1.0.\n\n· Using a separate game object targeting the bones with root transform and target transform.\n\n· Tweaking all the options offered by VRC Rotation Constraint and enabling \"Is Animated\" in Phys Bones.\n\n❌ Unsuccessful test scenario 1: VRC Rotation Constraint:\n\n· Lock Yes, Freeze Rotation Axes All OFF.\n\n· Lock No, Freeze Rotation Axes All OFF.\n\nThe Phys Bones work, but the rotation constraint doesn't. However, when I move my avatar, the bone never returns to its original rotation (X = -90) when it stops moving. It deforms continuously.\n\n· Lock yes, Freeze Rotation Axes All ON.\n\n· Lock no, Freeze Rotation Axes All ON.\n\n❌ Physbones doesn't work.\n\n❌Rotation constraint does work.\n\nvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvv\n\n✅ SUCCESSFUL TEST SCENARIO 2:\n\n> I finally got it working! 😸\n\n🦴 We need a dummy parent bone, which we'll call bone.root.R, and a child bone, bone.child.R, which contains the weightpaint. \n\n⚙️ Physbone configuration:\n\n· Root Transform: bone.root.R\n\n· Multi Child Type: First (this is very important; any other configuration won't work). ❗\n\n· Is Animated: OFF (even if it's on, it still works; turn it off for better performance).\n\nThe physics result is somewhat \"harder and heavier,\" but with some configuration, you can achieve a result similar to the original without rotation constraints.\n\n⚙️ VRC Rotation Constraint Configuration:\n\n· Is Active: Yes\n\n· Weight: 0.5 (or whatever you need)\n\n· Lock: Yes and Freeze Rotation Axes: ALL: Yes.\n\n· Sources: 1, the bone you need to aim.\n\n· Advanced settings:\n\n· Target Transform: bone.child.R\n\nI hope this research helps fix this bug and is useful for those who were looking for this option to work.\n\nBest regards. 💙",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
